WEBVTT

00:02.117 --> 00:05.766
[Love is the best teacher.]

00:05.767 --> 00:12.012
[Love is the best teacher.]
[Pliny the Younger, Epistulae]

00:17.180 --> 00:19.703
This is the latest in the series?

00:19.766 --> 00:24.195
Yes, I'd really like to get your thoughts on it.

00:24.781 --> 00:26.101
You've read it already?

00:26.367 --> 00:29.515
I couldn't put it down.

00:30.039 --> 00:34.382
When you're finished, you can just return
it to the library, if you don't mind.

00:35.508 --> 00:38.140
By the way, I'll just come out and ask.

00:38.247 --> 00:42.023
You're the one who got Ryuuen
to change, aren't you?

00:42.773 --> 00:44.544
Why do you think that?

00:45.117 --> 00:47.923
I've just put the pieces of the puzzle together.

00:50.508 --> 00:53.187
Sorry for being so forward.

00:53.523 --> 00:57.710
I'm sure you don't want to talk about this.

00:58.719 --> 01:04.711
I finally found a friend with similar interests,
and I'd hate to ruin that over this.

01:05.643 --> 01:10.057
But I realized if I didn't make a move,
things couldn't progress any further.

01:10.534 --> 01:12.447
Progress further?

01:12.604 --> 01:17.322
Sorry! Now that I say it out loud,
it doesn't make much sense to me, either.

01:18.815 --> 01:24.018
Um, I wanted to ask what you thought of
how Class D handled the last exam…

01:24.651 --> 01:27.057
I won't deny anything, at least.

01:27.698 --> 01:33.447
But it's clearly out of line to do something
that puts your opponent out of commission.

01:33.552 --> 01:36.588
You knew that, and you still didn't stop him?

01:36.838 --> 01:41.025
Do you think he'd listen politely
to anything I have to say?

01:43.783 --> 01:48.884
Will you give Ryuuen a message for me, Hiyori?

01:48.984 --> 01:50.986
[I'll be waiting at the Keyaki Mall Cafe.
Let me know if you can't come.]
Yes, anything!

01:51.705 --> 01:55.345
"Come here"? Uh, what for?

03:38.823 --> 03:39.689
Hey.

03:40.252 --> 03:41.861
What's this about?

03:42.143 --> 03:43.640
Wanna sit?

03:44.135 --> 03:48.455
People are gonna talk if they see
you chatting over tea with me.

03:53.307 --> 03:55.152
Who were you here with?

03:55.237 --> 03:57.654
Oh, it was Hiyori.

03:57.729 --> 03:58.846
Hiyo…?!

03:59.354 --> 04:01.354
We both like reading,

04:01.909 --> 04:03.697
so we have a lot to talk about.

04:04.229 --> 04:07.557
Wow, you're on a first-name basis and everything.

04:07.971 --> 04:10.135
Same hobby, huh.

04:11.065 --> 04:12.603
Wow…

04:15.838 --> 04:19.135
I guess you can hang out
with whoever, but like,

04:19.136 --> 04:21.260
what's this urgent business of yours?

04:21.510 --> 04:24.603
Sorry, I forgot what it was.

04:24.791 --> 04:26.596
Huh?! What the heck?

04:27.268 --> 04:29.674
I'll call you if I remember.

04:29.963 --> 04:32.267
You must have a screw loose or something.

04:32.643 --> 04:33.682
I'm leaving.

04:39.737 --> 04:43.439
Classy little place for a meeting.

04:43.815 --> 04:46.861
I heard what you did in the last exam.

04:47.377 --> 04:49.539
Are you back to your old ways, then?

04:49.612 --> 04:53.168
Who knows. Maybe the impulse just struck me.

04:54.205 --> 04:57.205
Then, what's your plan going forward?

04:57.737 --> 05:01.932
Don't think you can play
double agent and get your way.

05:02.768 --> 05:04.392
Dirty little bat.

05:05.424 --> 05:06.556
Double agent?

05:07.034 --> 05:11.182
Sorry, I'm not gonna stop at just two classes.

05:13.034 --> 05:14.244
Kanzaki?

05:15.026 --> 05:18.471
He wanted to see you no matter what.

05:19.002 --> 05:22.299
So you're trying to leverage that
to get an in with Class B?

05:22.651 --> 05:25.174
You think Kanzaki's gonna go for that?

05:25.557 --> 05:28.203
He will. Isn't that right?

05:28.690 --> 05:29.752
Hashimoto.

05:30.159 --> 05:35.210
I don't exactly trust you.
But you do have some utility to me.

05:36.166 --> 05:37.338
You see?

05:37.963 --> 05:42.392
So, will you regale me with
tales of crushing defeat?

05:43.409 --> 05:49.474
I'll tell you now that Class B won't fall for
underhanded tactics like that ever again.

05:49.909 --> 05:54.908
You're just Ichinose's lackey. What can you do?

05:55.323 --> 05:59.783
I may have spent this year
supporting Ichinose, yes.

06:00.049 --> 06:03.142
But if she's not willing to go to extremes,

06:04.049 --> 06:09.057
I have a different way of
dealing with people like you.

06:16.424 --> 06:17.682
Ayanokouji!

06:17.776 --> 06:18.658
What are you…?!

06:18.987 --> 06:23.885
Hey, Ayanokouji, I thought of
a great plan to get to Class A!

06:24.393 --> 06:27.137
You should just join our class!

06:27.221 --> 06:30.236
What?! What do you think you're doing?!

06:30.518 --> 06:33.807
If Ryuuen and Ayanokouji teamed up,
they'd be unstoppable!

06:34.205 --> 06:37.236
They could take down Sakayanagi and Ichinose both!

06:37.502 --> 06:39.424
I'm not against it, really.

06:40.377 --> 06:42.379
Are you… serious?

06:42.444 --> 06:45.590
See, I knew it! We welcome you with open arms!

06:45.754 --> 06:47.980
It's not realistically possible, though.

06:48.176 --> 06:51.574
How would you get 20 million
points for a class transfer?

06:52.004 --> 06:57.113
Besides, from where I'm standing, why
join forces when being rivals is more fun?

06:58.252 --> 07:01.525
You and Ryuuen are both total freaks.

07:02.939 --> 07:04.447
Yeah, maybe.

07:12.400 --> 07:15.283
You'll catch a cold hanging around out here.

07:15.791 --> 07:17.306
Ayanokouji.

07:18.994 --> 07:22.501
You're pushier than I thought, you know.

07:22.908 --> 07:26.470
Seems like you don't wanna go
back to your own dorm, that's all.

07:27.486 --> 07:32.743
I feel like you always show up
in my moments of weakness.

07:33.193 --> 07:37.207
If you want, you can vent to me again.

07:37.748 --> 07:42.575
No way, I've been putting way too much on you.

07:43.318 --> 07:45.614
I can't just keep unloading on you…

07:46.466 --> 07:48.544
It's unbecoming of me. I can't.

07:49.365 --> 07:51.130
Don't you trust me?

07:51.435 --> 07:52.722
Of course I do!

07:53.045 --> 07:58.833
I think… I trust you more
than anyone else right now.

07:59.099 --> 08:01.731
Even though we're in competing classes?

08:02.037 --> 08:04.903
I can't just simply write you off as an enemy.

08:05.248 --> 08:09.896
We're not on the same side.
But you're someone I can trust.

08:14.646 --> 08:18.357
The other day when I was
talking to Horikita, it hit me.

08:18.873 --> 08:21.802
She's grown so much this year.

08:22.154 --> 08:25.021
Same with Ryuuen, and Sakayanagi.

08:25.818 --> 08:29.318
The ringleaders of every class
are growing stronger.

08:30.865 --> 08:33.989
I wonder if I still stand a chance against them…

08:34.974 --> 08:38.357
I'm scared. Where will I be a year from now?

08:39.537 --> 08:43.130
I just… don't know what to do.

08:49.646 --> 08:51.716
Ayanokouji…?

08:52.974 --> 08:56.443
You're hard to figure out, Ayanokouji.

08:57.021 --> 09:02.044
Hey, Ichinose. Do you want to
meet here again one year from now?

09:02.278 --> 09:03.802
Just the two of us.

09:07.242 --> 09:11.570
Keep pushing forward with confidence
next year, then come and see me.

09:12.101 --> 09:13.609
Can you promise that?

09:14.203 --> 09:18.624
But, by then… I might be…

09:18.859 --> 09:20.398
my class might…

09:20.413 --> 09:21.577
It doesn't matter.

09:22.397 --> 09:28.170
I want to tell you something,
and I promise I'll tell you then.

09:28.632 --> 09:30.632
Okay, I'll promise you, too.

09:30.929 --> 09:32.947
I'll give it my all next year!

09:33.210 --> 09:35.670
And I'll be aiming for Class A!

09:36.491 --> 09:39.663
The future isn't set in stone, but…

09:40.436 --> 09:43.623
if Ichinose is defeated,

09:44.561 --> 09:45.960
when that time comes,

09:46.639 --> 09:48.319
I'll deal the finishing blow.

09:48.963 --> 09:53.968
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

09:56.184 --> 09:57.972
This place brings back memories.

09:58.285 --> 09:59.722
Enough small talk.

10:00.012 --> 10:01.730
What's this message from Hiyori mean, Ayanokouji?

10:01.730 --> 10:03.472
[Ayanokouji says he would have handled
the exam better! Also, please talk to him.]
What's this message from Hiyori mean, Ayanokouji?

10:03.473 --> 10:04.792
What's this message from Hiyori mean, Ayanokouji?

10:05.019 --> 10:06.566
Just what it sounds like.

10:06.840 --> 10:10.253
You think you could do better, play it safer?

10:11.074 --> 10:16.191
I'll miss you if you mess up and
have to leave the school, that's all.

10:17.027 --> 10:21.621
That's big talk for the guy
who just lost to Sakayanagi.

10:21.863 --> 10:23.503
I did lose,

10:23.777 --> 10:27.831
and there's no excuse for that as a leader.

10:28.098 --> 10:30.425
What? Are you mocking me?

10:30.887 --> 10:34.628
You beat me. Sakayanagi can't be better than you.

10:35.105 --> 10:37.894
Either your head wasn't in the game to start with,

10:38.926 --> 10:42.316
or maybe it was an accident beyond your control.

10:42.691 --> 10:44.003
Am I wrong?

10:47.463 --> 10:50.791
So, what's your plan now?

10:50.869 --> 10:53.541
I'll take it easy and enjoy my time off.

10:53.948 --> 10:59.252
Then, when I get bored of that, I'll start
warming up to take down Ichinose and Sakayanagi.

10:59.315 --> 11:03.478
And then, if anyone can get you expelled,

11:04.872 --> 11:06.325
it's gotta be me!

11:11.958 --> 11:13.423
You're doing too much.

11:14.242 --> 11:16.578
I had the element of surprise, too.

11:17.930 --> 11:19.930
You've got potential.

11:20.281 --> 11:24.085
So I want to see you get better, Ryuuen.

11:24.523 --> 11:27.812
Who the hell died and made you my teacher?

11:28.328 --> 11:34.734
If someone gets proof of what you pulled
against Class B, you'll be screwed.

11:35.474 --> 11:39.567
As it stands, we might not
even get to have a rematch.

11:40.825 --> 11:43.770
Stop doing things that are
easy to trace back to you.

11:44.380 --> 11:48.286
I'll take your shitty advice
into consideration for now.

11:48.576 --> 11:51.763
But rest assured, I will destroy you.

11:54.646 --> 11:57.958
I wouldn't mind being destroyed at your hand.

11:59.435 --> 12:02.380
You've been going on a lot of dates with Ike, huh?

12:02.552 --> 12:05.630
Huh?! I wouldn't be caught dead dating him!

12:05.818 --> 12:07.966
No need to deny it.

12:07.974 --> 12:09.644
I was curious about that, too!

12:09.645 --> 12:11.645
I'm telling you, it's not like that!

12:11.646 --> 12:14.895
Oh, really now? Then why are you blushing?

12:15.349 --> 12:17.091
All the way to your ears!

12:17.130 --> 12:20.278
Okay, that's enough! Give me a break!

12:20.318 --> 12:22.067
Well, on one condition…

12:22.068 --> 12:23.888
Sorry. Something urgent came up.

12:24.162 --> 12:26.122
I've gotta go. Later!

12:26.872 --> 12:28.239
Oh, sure.

12:29.076 --> 12:31.919
Karuizawa seems kinda off.

12:32.138 --> 12:34.138
I wonder if something happened.

12:34.888 --> 12:38.380
Come to think of it, Satou,
what happened with Ayanokouji?

12:39.020 --> 12:42.918
Oh, right! You were trying to decide
whether to tell him how you feel!

12:44.013 --> 12:46.161
Keep this between us, okay?

12:46.357 --> 12:47.443
Of course, girl!

12:47.470 --> 12:48.641
We won't tell a soul.

12:52.476 --> 12:55.389
What?! He shot you down just like that?!

12:55.554 --> 12:57.632
K-Keep your voice down!

12:57.663 --> 13:00.460
Is he some kind of moron?

13:00.546 --> 13:05.530
Ayanokouji… probably likes Karuizawa, I think.

13:05.593 --> 13:06.100
Huh?

13:06.140 --> 13:07.905
L-Like, for real?

13:09.226 --> 13:11.069
And Karuizawa…

13:11.734 --> 13:15.468
probably likes him back, too.

13:16.531 --> 13:19.173
I'm trying to forget it and move on, you know?

13:19.679 --> 13:24.593
Karuizawa's always looking for
a high-value man, though, isn't she?

13:24.945 --> 13:29.522
Hey, wait! Ayanokouji is pretty amazing, actually!

13:29.577 --> 13:32.725
What, you mean 'cause he can run fast?

13:32.952 --> 13:35.952
Well, yeah, but it's not just that.

13:38.499 --> 13:41.460
What's this about? Why are we here?

13:41.859 --> 13:43.445
What do you say?

13:43.725 --> 13:48.077
How would you like to go back to your
dear father when spring break is over?

13:48.726 --> 13:51.624
I like being at this school.

13:52.062 --> 13:58.132
In that case, your school career is
only going to get more difficult.

13:58.374 --> 14:00.663
Shall we play a little game?

14:01.632 --> 14:07.530
We've selected one person from the White Room
to enroll as a student here for the next term.

14:08.228 --> 14:14.149
If you can determine who it is before
the end of April, I will resign my position.

14:14.571 --> 14:21.165
That student will be the one to break it to you
that you are no longer our only success story.

14:21.353 --> 14:27.571
I accept. But there's one thing
I can say for certain.

14:28.610 --> 14:33.415
There is no more outstanding person to
come out of the White Room than me.

14:34.032 --> 14:38.235
Those uncanny eyes, shrouded
in impenetrable darkness…

14:38.431 --> 14:40.969
You take after your father.

14:43.806 --> 14:45.516
Ayanokouji?

14:50.173 --> 14:52.360
Do you need something, Matsushita?

14:53.251 --> 14:54.454
What is it?

14:54.837 --> 14:57.180
Were you talking to the chairman just now?

14:57.571 --> 15:02.938
They're thinking about renovating this area,
and I passed by, so he asked my opinion.

15:03.407 --> 15:05.758
Oh, I see.

15:09.407 --> 15:15.539
Hey, I got the answer you helped with right on
the mental arithmetic test the other day.

15:19.436 --> 15:22.108
It's one of my better subjects, I guess.

15:22.671 --> 15:27.740
I saw you, though. Talking to Hirata on the bench.

15:34.210 --> 15:37.709
He didn't just happen to feel better
out of nowhere, did he?

15:38.741 --> 15:43.108
Ayanokouji, aren't you better at
school and sports than you let on?

15:43.694 --> 15:46.897
I hold back because I don't want to stand out.

15:47.022 --> 15:50.225
Then, I want you to contribute to the class more.

15:50.968 --> 15:54.084
I want to aim for Class A, too.

15:54.717 --> 15:57.483
That's what I was thinking about doing anyway.

15:57.796 --> 15:58.639
Huh?

15:58.749 --> 16:01.748
But, don't get your hopes up too much.

16:02.530 --> 16:05.037
I'm giving around 70 or 80 percent.

16:05.936 --> 16:07.014
Got it.

16:07.936 --> 16:10.631
Oh, and one more thing.

16:13.890 --> 16:15.391
[Call this contact?]

16:17.561 --> 16:19.733
I wanted to ask you about Karuizawa.

16:20.803 --> 16:25.498
If Karuizawa knows what you're capable of,
does that mean you see her as special?

16:25.827 --> 16:27.303
No, it's not like that.

16:27.514 --> 16:30.600
Okay, then what's going on between you two?

16:32.033 --> 16:34.035
[Call this contact?]

16:36.991 --> 16:38.194
What is it?

16:38.561 --> 16:44.233
We're aiming for Class A next year. I wonder if
I might convince you to show your true abilities.

16:44.694 --> 16:45.717
I'll pass.

16:46.046 --> 16:46.912
Why?

16:47.257 --> 16:51.826
Sorry, but there's no one in our year
who stands a chance against me.

16:52.139 --> 16:54.201
There's no point in going all out.

16:54.796 --> 16:56.740
Then, let's test that theory.

16:56.866 --> 16:58.319
How would we do that?

16:59.163 --> 17:04.138
Why don't we compete on a written exam
when we enter our second year?

17:04.288 --> 17:05.756
[Ayanokouji Kiyotaka]

17:05.757 --> 17:09.959
[Ayanokouji Kiyotaka]
If I win, you have to join the student council.

17:09.960 --> 17:10.233
[Ayanokouji Kiyotaka]

17:11.655 --> 17:14.435
May I ask why those are your terms?

17:14.928 --> 17:17.631
I'll tell you why when you lose.

17:18.099 --> 17:19.537
I'd rather not.

17:20.474 --> 17:25.974
When I win, I'll have you work to
your full abilities from then on.

17:26.435 --> 17:27.396
Okay.

17:27.560 --> 17:29.250
I'll be looking forward to it.

17:29.483 --> 17:30.225
See you.

18:58.508 --> 18:59.922
Okay, what?

19:00.422 --> 19:03.375
Did you finally remember what
you were gonna tell me?

19:03.453 --> 19:04.770
Calm down.

19:04.969 --> 19:09.148
I already told you, I have
dinner plans with my friends at 7.

19:09.250 --> 19:10.414
Got it?

19:10.719 --> 19:12.156
There's plenty of time.

19:14.743 --> 19:17.345
Your vibes are like, totally off.

19:17.859 --> 19:21.540
Like you've been stalling or whatever
since that time at the cafe.

19:21.938 --> 19:27.383
Oh, right! And Satou's been getting all kinds
of weird ideas about us, by the way!

19:28.063 --> 19:32.062
Matsushita has suspicions that
something's going on between us, too.

19:32.422 --> 19:33.984
What? Are you for real?

19:34.164 --> 19:37.656
She also has suspicions about my abilities.

19:38.508 --> 19:43.601
I assume she's also the type to
hide her above-average abilities.

19:43.767 --> 19:45.767
H-Hang on a sec!

19:46.165 --> 19:48.993
This is a lot to get my head around.

19:49.056 --> 19:51.940
I don't like where this is going, though.

19:52.056 --> 19:56.727
I mean, can't we just leave
Satou and Matsushita be?

19:57.236 --> 19:59.150
No, we absolutely can't!

19:59.681 --> 20:04.200
If word gets around, this is all
gonna come back to bite me.

20:04.759 --> 20:05.790
You think so?

20:06.743 --> 20:09.618
If I want to find love again,

20:09.977 --> 20:14.219
no one's gonna approach me if they
think there's another guy in the picture.

20:17.681 --> 20:22.016
I broke up with Hirata, so now
I'm looking for a new boyfriend.

20:22.054 --> 20:23.165
Is that a problem?

20:23.900 --> 20:24.970
No, it's not.

20:25.837 --> 20:28.829
You've been getting all cozy
with Shiina lately, too!

20:29.243 --> 20:32.188
And she likes the same stuff you do, unlike me!

20:37.103 --> 20:38.540
Anyway, I'm leaving!

20:39.540 --> 20:40.258
Kei.

20:40.454 --> 20:41.454
What?

20:42.517 --> 20:46.852
If you don't want to, you can
forget I said anything, but…

20:47.650 --> 20:48.524
Huh?

20:49.508 --> 20:50.880
Will you go out with me?

20:52.493 --> 20:56.048
I'm asking you if you want to date me.

20:57.845 --> 20:59.380
I get that, I just…!

20:59.548 --> 21:01.719
I'm just… kinda…

21:04.345 --> 21:07.227
…confused, I guess?

21:07.946 --> 21:10.352
I mean, what? Huh?!

21:10.962 --> 21:14.485
What are you playing at? Aren't you and Shiina…

21:14.486 --> 21:19.025
I just wanted to see if that
would make you jealous, Kei.

21:19.259 --> 21:23.345
Wh… What the heck? Where did that come from?!

21:23.759 --> 21:29.111
I don't want you to be someone else's girlfriend.

21:29.822 --> 21:33.827
So, like, are you saying that…

21:38.616 --> 21:40.725
…you like me?

21:41.022 --> 21:44.819
Yeah. I like you, Karuizawa Kei.

21:51.366 --> 21:54.342
I-I'll go out with you, I guess!

21:54.421 --> 21:58.053
Can I assume that means you like me back?

21:59.218 --> 22:01.733
Y-You're gonna make me say it?

22:02.100 --> 22:03.834
Yeah, I am.

22:04.249 --> 22:06.733
Well, like…

22:07.319 --> 22:12.299
Okay, I… like you too.

22:13.158 --> 22:14.713
Unfortunately.

22:16.409 --> 22:17.408
Whoa!

22:19.158 --> 22:21.940
D-Don't tell me you're gonna kiss me or something!

22:22.510 --> 22:25.424
I'm not. Not yet.

22:25.651 --> 22:27.494
N-Not yet?!

22:29.253 --> 22:31.346
This should be okay for now, right?

22:34.167 --> 22:36.815
Fine, I'll allow it.

22:40.901 --> 22:44.026
Hey, did you get a little taller?

22:44.925 --> 22:46.299
I might have.

22:48.667 --> 22:52.229
People are always learning and growing.

22:52.643 --> 22:56.994
Karuizawa Kei has to experience
this kind of love to grow.

22:57.628 --> 23:02.432
Likewise, I can learn about love through her.

23:03.058 --> 23:06.362
The things I couldn't learn in the White Room.

23:06.932 --> 23:10.869
But once she's served her purpose as a textbook,

23:11.010 --> 23:12.932
she'll be of no more use to me.

23:14.260 --> 23:15.463
Or maybe…

23:16.401 --> 23:19.533
the future has something else in store for me.

23:20.893 --> 23:23.229
Either way, I hope…

23:26.503 --> 23:32.026
Right now, standing here holding
someone who's important to me…

